---
title: HL-RCS — Google Sign In and First-time Registration (Web)
---
sequenceDiagram
autonumber
actor U as Guest
participant UI as «user interaction» AuthPage / GoogleSignIn
participant G as «external» Google Identity Services
participant C as «control» AuthController
participant S as «service» AuthServiceImpl
participant V as «security» GoogleTokenVerifier
participant R as «entity» User / Capability Repositories
participant J as «security» JwtTokenProvider
U->>UI: Choose Sign in with Google
UI->>+G: Open account selection and authentication
G-->>-UI: Credential (Google ID token)
UI->>+C: POST /api/auth/google (idToken)
C->>+S: loginWithGoogle(request)
S->>+V: verifyToken(idToken)
V->>V: Verify signature, issuer, audience, expiry,<br/>verified email and subject
V-->>-S: GoogleUserInfo or exception
alt Invalid token or Google not configured
S-->>C: AppException (401 / 503)
C-->>UI: Error response
UI-->>U: Display sign-in error
else Valid Google identity
S->>+R: findByGoogleSubject(subject)
R-->>-S: User or null
alt No account for Google subject
S->>+R: existsByEmail(normalized email)
R-->>-S: Exists?
alt Email belongs to another account
S->>S: Reject automatic account linking (409)
else Email available
S->>S: Build USER, ACTIVE, GOOGLE account;<br/>encode random password; set Google subject
S->>+R: saveAndFlush(user)
R-->>-S: Saved user or uniqueness violation (409)
end
else Existing Google account
S->>S: Require ACTIVE status; otherwise 403
end
alt Conflict or inactive account
S-->>C: AppException (409 / 403)
C-->>UI: Error response; no session
UI-->>U: Display conflict or account restriction
else Eligible user
S->>+R: Find ACTIVE capabilities
R-->>-S: Capability codes
S->>+J: generateTokenFromUser(user)
J-->>-S: Application JWT
S-->>C: AuthResponse; commit
C-->>UI: HTTP 200 — ApiResponse of AuthResponse
UI->>UI: acceptSession(data, remember)
UI-->>U: Enter application
end
end
deactivate S
deactivate C
